# Words this machine must never publish, one per line, as "label = regex".
#
# Copy this file to .private-words and fill in your own values. That copy is
# ignored by git on purpose. A deny list that ships with the repository would
# publish exactly the values it is meant to protect.
#
# The structural patterns, such as private IP ranges, mail addresses and phone
# numbers, are built into tools/check-private.py and need no entry here. This
# file is for the literals only you know about.

# host name = ^$
# home network = ^$
# user name = ^$
# employer = ^$
